  <title>
    <media type="image" width="40px" height="40px" its:translate="no" src="figures/orca-logo.svg" /> Say All
  </title>
  <p>
    Say All speaks document content continuously from your current location.
  </p>
  <p>
    The settings below control continuous presentation and navigation during Say All. For
    presenting the visible contents of a window or dialog, see "<link xref="features_reviewing_objects_flat_review">Flat review</link>".
  </p>
  <section id="settings-say-all">
    <title>Settings</title>
    <p>
      <em style="strong">Preferences location:</em>
      <gui>Say All</gui> category.
    </p>
    <p>
      <em style="strong">Available settings:</em>
    </p>
    <list>
      <item>
        <p>
          <gui>Say All By</gui>: Say All reads from the
          current location to the end of the document; this controls whether it reads by
          sentence or by line. Choices: Sentence, Line.
        </p>
        <list>
          <item>
            <p>
              <gui>Sentence (default)</gui>: Reads a sentence
              at a time.
            </p>
          </item>
          <item>
            <p>
              <gui>Line</gui>: Reads a line at a time.
            </p>
          </item>
        </list>
      </item>
      <item>
        <p>
          <gui>Only speak displayed text</gui>: Speaks text
          without additional information such as object roles and change announcements. Default:
          off.
        </p>
      </item>
      <item>
        <p>
          <gui>Rewind and Fast Forward By</gui>: Controls which
          commands can move within the document while Say All is active.
        </p>
        <list>
          <item>
            <p>
              <gui>Up and down arrow</gui>: Controls whether
              Up Arrow and Down Arrow rewind and fast-forward during Say All instead of
              interrupting it. Default: off.
            </p>
          </item>
          <item>
            <p>
              <gui>Structural navigation</gui>: Controls whether
              structural navigation is available during Say All. Moving to another heading or
              other document element continues presentation from there. Default: off.
            </p>
          </item>
        </list>
      </item>
      <item>
        <p>
          <gui>Change Announcements</gui>: Controls which
          document revision and text formatting changes Orca announces during Say All.
        </p>
        <list>
          <item>
            <p>
              <gui>Tracked changes</gui>: Controls whether
              Orca announces tracked changes such as insertions, deletions, highlights, and
              suggestions. Default: on.
            </p>
          </item>
        </list>
      </item>
      <item>
        <p>
          <gui>Container Announcements</gui>: Controls which
          document and web-container boundaries Orca announces during Say All.
        </p>
        <list>
          <item>
            <p>
              <gui>Articles</gui>: Controls whether Orca
              announces articles. Default: on.
            </p>
          </item>
          <item>
            <p>
              <gui>Blockquotes</gui>: Controls whether
              Orca announces blockquotes. Default: on.
            </p>
          </item>
          <item>
            <p>
              <gui>Code blocks</gui>: Controls whether
              Orca announces code blocks. Default: on.
            </p>
          </item>
          <item>
            <p>
              <gui>Embedded documents</gui>: Controls whether
              Orca announces documents embedded within an application. Default: on.
            </p>
          </item>
          <item>
            <p>
              <gui>Forms</gui>: Controls whether Orca
              announces forms. Default: on.
            </p>
          </item>
          <item>
            <p>
              <gui>Headers and footers</gui>: Controls whether
              Orca announces headers and footers. Default: on. Available in Orca 52 and later.
            </p>
          </item>
          <item>
            <p>
              <gui>Landmarks</gui>: Controls whether Orca
              announces landmarks, named regions of a page such as navigation or main content.
              Default: on.
            </p>
          </item>
          <item>
            <p>
              <gui>Lists</gui>: Controls whether Orca
              announces lists. Default: on.
            </p>
          </item>
          <item>
            <p>
              <gui>Panels</gui>: Controls whether Orca
              announces panels. Default: on.
            </p>
          </item>
          <item>
            <p>
              <gui>Tables</gui>: Controls whether Orca
              announces tables. Default: on.
            </p>
          </item>
        </list>
      </item>
    </list>
  </section>
  <section id="commands-say-all">
    <title>Commands</title>
    <p>
      <em style="strong">Preferences location:</em>
      <gui>Commands</gui> category, <gui>Commands</gui> section, <gui>Say All</gui> group.
    </p>
    <list>
      <item>
        <p>
          <gui>Speak entire document</gui>
        </p>
        <list>
          <item>
            <p>
              Desktop: <keyseq>
                <key>Keypad Add</key>
              </keyseq>
            </p>
          </item>
          <item>
            <p>
              Laptop: <keyseq>
                <key>Orca Modifier</key>
                <key>Semicolon</key>
              </keyseq>
            </p>
          </item>
        </list>
        <p>
          Starts continuous presentation from the current location. Press a key to interrupt it;
          enabled navigation options can instead move within the content.
        </p>
      </item>
    </list>
  </section>
